{"repositoryId":1345842700,"availability":"available","full":"mikroverk/esp32sim","name":"esp32sim","description":"Open-source ESP32 emulator. Run real firmware locally or in your browser — no hardware, no cloud, no subscription.","category":"Other","language":"Rust","stars":432,"forks":24,"created":"2026-08-25T07:51:17Z","updated":"2026-10-19T22:08:59Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":[],"demo":"https://mikroverk.github.io/esp32sim/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T22:16:20.487Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T22:16:20.487Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T22:16:20.487Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T22:16:20.487Z","discoveredVia":[],"metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-19T22:16:20.487Z","stars":432,"forks":24}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["esp32sim is an ESP32 emulator written in Rust. It runs real ESP32 firmware on your computer or in a browser tab, without the hardware.","It boots the chip's own mask ROM, the real second-stage bootloader and your unmodified application. It also models the board around the chip: displays, touch, LEDs, buttons, audio, camera and WiFi."],"features":["The full boot chain: mask ROM, bootloader, FreeRTOS, then your app. No patched firmware.","WiFi with the unmodified Espressif WiFi library. Firmware joins a virtual access point, gets","DHCP, DNS and NTP, and can reach the real network, HTTPS included.","Board models, so firmware can draw on a display, read touch, light LEDs and play sound.","Speed: the S3 has a block cache and a JIT, and runs helloworld about 30 times faster than real"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mikroverk/esp32sim/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"d3c164159dcb464c838eb5bfb2749d9bb8c3de44b368997f1a7927f3443394f1","extractedAt":"2026-10-19T22:16:20.487Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T22:16:20.487Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"esp32sim is an ESP32 emulator written in Rust. It runs real ESP32 firmwa